Package: cybroid-edition-classroom
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: CybroidOS maintainers <citos@cybroid.com>
Homepage: https://cybroid.com/cybroidos
Section: metapackages
Priority: optional
Depends: cybroid-plasma (>= @VERSION@), veyon-service, veyon-master, kiwix, gcompris-qt, tuxpaint, tuxmath, ktouch, kturtle, thonny, kbruch, cantor, kalzium, avogadro, step, stellarium, marble, kgeography, parley, openboard, audacity
Description: CybroidOS Classroom: for school computer rooms
 Every lab computer the same and ready for the next class: Veyon lets
 the teacher see, lock and guide every screen; student accounts in the
 "lab" group are reset to a clean state at each start. Scratch and
 GeoGebra, as schools everywhere use them; Kiwix opens Wikipedia and other
 libraries without the internet; OpenBoard is an interactive whiteboard
 for the teacher. Also: GCompris, Tux Paint and TuxMath for young
 learners; KTouch for typing; KTurtle and Thonny for programming; KBruch
 and Cantor for mathematics; Kalzium and Avogadro for chemistry; Step for
 physics; Stellarium for astronomy; Marble and KGeography for geography;
 Parley for vocabulary; Audacity for recording.
 .
 The same CybroidOS as every edition (look, updates, Hangar), with these
 tools added. Chosen in the welcome at first sign-in, or later in Settings
 (any number of editions together), and installed from deb.cybroid.com.
